  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1035 AM MDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nMean upper troughing over the PAC NW and western Canada will \nsupport general SW flow through the remainder week with weak/dry \nimpulses traversing the flow. Departing impulse giving way to \nclear skies today as winds shifts NW behind the sfc reflection. \nExpect highs in the 50s and 60s. Otherwise, for the rest of the \nweek highs will generally be in the 60s, although things will cool\ndown Friday some behind a weak cool front, with highs generally \nin the 50s that day. Mild this weekend as WAA and height rises \nspread NE ahead of the digging western CONUS upper trough. There \nis a low chance for a few showers Friday night toward central SD \nas a disturbance skirts the region and forces pos theta-e adv. \nWestern CONUS upper trough will lift out the Pac NW early next \nweek, with broad lift spreading into the region starting Sunday \nnight. The best chance for precip will be Monday when the main \ntrough passes over the region. Very warm system for early Nov, \nwith mainly rain expected. However, enough cold air may entrain \ninto the back of the system Monday to allow for some higher \nelevation snow across northeast WY and the Black Hills. This could\nsome support some light snow accums chances there, esp in the \nnorthern Black Hills.",
